2. A method for reducing the cobalt content in an aqueous solution containing a cyanocobalt complex, the method comprising:
mixing an aqueous solution containing a cyanocobalt complex having a pH of less than 5.0 with a copper compound and a dithiocarbamate polymer, or mixing an aqueous solution containing a cyanocobalt complex having a pH of 5.0 or more with an acid, a copper compound, and a dithiocarbamate polymer, thereby generating a first precipitate in an acidic cobalt-containing aqueous solution having a pH of less than 5.0, and obtaining a cobalt-containing acidic aqueous solution including the first precipitate;
removing at least part of the first precipitate from the cobalt-containing acidic aqueous solution containing the first precipitate;
adjusting the pH of the cobalt-containing acidic aqueous solution, from which at least part of the first precipitate has been removed, to 8.0 or higher to generate a second precipitate; and
removing at least part of the second precipitate from the cobalt-containing basic aqueous solution containing the second precipitate.
